# Local, git-ignored make overrides — copy to `Makefile.local` and edit.
#
# `make arch` (luxarch), `make lint` (luxlint) and `make audit` (luxaudit) run
# private fleet guards that live on a private registry (internal tooling, not
# published). Set its host here so the value stays out of the public repo — the same
# pattern as .env.<env> and the nginx confs (committed *.example templates;
# real files git-ignored). All three guards read this one var (LUXARCH_REGISTRY).
#
# Contributors without registry access: `make test` and the import-linter contracts
# inside `make arch` still run; luxarch/luxlint/luxaudit (and thus the ruff+mypy of
# `make lint`) are simply skipped with a notice.
#
# LUXARCH_REGISTRY := your.registry.example:5000

# `make publish-sha` / `make dev-deploy` push each commit's images to the private
# registry. The image block requires a literal here (not `$(LUXARCH_REGISTRY)`): a
# value built from another variable takes whatever the shell gives that variable.
# Left unset, every target that pushes or pins refuses.
#
# REGISTRY := your.registry.example:5000

# `make smoke` (run by `make dev-deploy`) probes the deployed dev stack from
# outside. Point it at the address the dev stack answers on, and export
# SMOKE_AUTH_TOKEN (one of the stack's SECURITY__AUTH_TOKENS) in your shell for
# the authenticated probe.
#
# SMOKE_URL := https://luxswirl.dev.example
